<content>
  <section><para>A streaming service offers two options for subscription plans. Option A charges $10.99 a month plus $2 per movie. Option B charges $5.99 a month plus $3 per movie. The table below describes this. Which of the following systems of equations represents the two options for one month?</para>
<table>
  <tgroup cols="5"><thead>
    <row>
      <entry>\(x\) (Number of movies</entry>
      <entry>0</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
      <entry>2</entry>
      <entry>3</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>Option A</entry>
      <entry>10.99</entry>
      <entry>12.99</entry>
      <entry>14.99</entry>
      <entry>16.99</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>Option B</entry>
      <entry>5.99</entry>
      <entry>8.99</entry>
      <entry>11.99</entry>
      <entry>14.99</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</tgroup></table>
</section>
</content>
